@startuml
title Phase 6 LoRA Training And Promotion Gates

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Maintainer
participant "scripts.finetune" as CLI
participant "Dataset preflight" as Preflight
database "Phase 5 package" as Package
participant "Tokenizer" as Tokenizer
participant "Unsloth + TRL" as Trainer
database "checkpoints / adapter" as Artifacts
database "GGUF artifact" as GGUF
participant "Direct-adapter smoke test" as Smoke
participant "Phase 6 evaluation" as Evaluation

Maintainer -> CLI: finetune --config <versioned config>
CLI -> Preflight: check four configured paths exist
Preflight -> Package: read selected packaging-manifest fields
Preflight --> CLI: unverified counts and provenance summary
note right of Preflight
  No row parsing, count reconciliation,
  split-overlap check, or config schema.
  Test JSONL is not consumed by SFT.
end note
CLI -> Tokenizer: render chat exactly once
Tokenizer -> Tokenizer: append EOS; reject > max_length
CLI -> Trainer: train response-only LoRA
Trainer -> Package: read rendered train/validation text
Trainer -> Artifacts: checkpoints, then adapter
Trainer -> GGUF: save configured quantization
CLI -> Artifacts: write manifest only after GGUF succeeds
note right of Artifacts
  No resume_from_checkpoint support.
  Partial artifacts can lack a current manifest.
end note
Maintainer -> Smoke: load direct adapter; bounded hello + DFIR prompts
Smoke -> Artifacts: generate with model-defined stop-ID list
note right of Smoke
  Current test_lora.py points at v5 and runs only hello.
  It prints rather than enforces failure, and its
  stop-ID report still requires correction.
end note
alt termination and behavior gates pass
  Smoke --> Maintainer: eligible for promotion
  Maintainer -> GGUF: promote/serve generated artifact
  Maintainer -> Evaluation: run calibrated benchmark
else loops, template leakage, or token cap
  Smoke --> Maintainer: reject artifact and preserve for diagnosis
end

@enduml
